WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:09.480
Attorneys general from 48 states, Puerto
Rico, and DC recently announced that

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:13.019
they're investigating Google for
possible antitrust violations.

00:00:13.019 --> 00:00:18.480
The AG's want a say in how Google
manages advertising, uses AI, and displays

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:23.910
search results. Let's see: Attorneys with
political aspirations want to control

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:28.560
business strategy for one of the world's
most complex tech companies. what could

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:32.099
go wrong?
Plenty! Microsoft tried for years and

00:00:32.099 --> 00:00:36.059
hasn't achieved Google's quality. And if
the AG's take Google down a few notches,

00:00:36.059 --> 00:00:40.230
the cost to you will be three hundred
and eighty billion dollars annually in

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:44.040
lost search quality. And the
investigation doesn't look genuine. The

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:48.539
AG's have already said that Google is an
"existential threat", a "juggernaut", and that

00:00:48.539 --> 00:00:53.129
it takes away people's freedom. Who
benefits from the investigation? EU

00:00:53.129 --> 00:00:57.660
leaders: They've been trying for years to
hamstring US companies. And China's

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:02.670
leaders: Their tech companies are in hot
pursuit of the US. Let's hope the AG's

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:07.200
google "overconfidence" and realize they
can't improve tech services.

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:12.920
What do you think about the AG's investigation?
Should they proceed? Or should they drop

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:17.280
it? Let us know in our poll, and let us
know other topics that you'd like our

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:21.479
scholars to cover in 60 seconds, and be
sure to like and subscribe for more

00:01:21.479 --> 00:01:25.400
research and videos from AEI.

